# Vanilla web rules

- Use semantic HTML: `<header>`, `<main>`, `<nav>`, `<footer>`, `<article>`, `<section>`, `<aside>`.
- Prefer progressive enhancement: content works without JavaScript; JS adds interactivity.
- Use consistent class naming: BEM or kebab-case. Avoid inline styles for layout; use CSS classes.
- CSS variables for theming (colors, spacing, typography); reference pn-design-system for token structure.
- A11y: one `<h1>` per page, labels for form controls, logical heading order, focus order.
- Responsive and touch: mobile-first; min 44×48px touch targets; no hover-only for critical actions; never disable zoom.
- Keep JS minimal; no unnecessary libraries unless required by the feature.
